== (A) every feature that could stop the 1450PF going lower
  rib catch at the rib top, frame and case nominal: end walls +0.012, long walls -0.748 (positive = the rib is under the frame's bottom edge)
  rib stands proud of its wall by 0.76 at its top: the frame's bottom edge must land in that band, and the frame outline and
  the case interior each move it by +-0.38 per side, so no frame size is caught by the ribs across both tolerances
  shoulder Z 101.04: cavity below it 381.00 x 266.70; frame widest 378.96 x 263.14 (+0.76: 379.72 x 263.90): clear by 0.26 / 1.02 per side at the worst
  rim Z 108.97 and the lid tongue: nothing on the frame reaches outboard of 378.96 x 263.14, so neither can carry it
  the gasket step (#1488, frame z 5.46) and its o-ring: the o-ring goes in after the frame is screwed (instruction step 4), so it holds nothing
  vertical corners: case R 15.88 (#595) against the frame's R 16.51 (#3257): gap on the diagonal 2.26, larger than the sides
  walls alone, end walls (the frame's widest line meets the drafted wall): frame bottom Z 63.12
  walls alone, long walls: frame bottom Z 41.35

