  east: every plug's cable leaves along the wall toward its bundle's end, the plug turned 30 degrees down; the cables run in a bundle 4.98 x 4.98 over the pack's
  outer strip in the slot under the plugs (Z 46.80..51.78), in the lane between B16's edge and the legs' columns, and go down beyond the legs
  front bundle: 5G MAIN, 5G DIV, 5G ANT3, IRIDIUM; back bundle: LORA; west: every cable leaves downward and falls to the floor outboard of B16's edge
  each east cable (the class's reach 16.0, turned 30 degrees): its ferrule ends at 13.86 along the wall and Z 51.00, it lands at 20.11 from its site, Z 49.33, the band's middle; the layers' centres are Z 48.045 and 50.535; the neighbour's axis is at 31
  the drop keeps 8.32 from the next plug's body; a cable in the band's upper layer passes under that body with 2.22
  as laid out under 5G MAIN (3 passing: 5G DIV, 5G ANT3, IRIDIUM): the passing cables in the band's lower layer and its inner upper place, 5G MAIN's own cable in the outer upper place
  at the class's reach it lands 1.21 below that place, onto the passing cable under it; it lands at its place for a reach of 13.58 or less, or turned 26.5 degrees; the inner upper place clears the ferrule's end only for a ferrule 2.58 across or less (the class does not bound it)
  the inboard column, with the plug's cable axis at its inner end (X 172.63): inner face X 168.89, 3.89 from B16's edge (-0.38 at the worst); with the axis 4.0 from that end 7.89 (3.62); met at the worst for an axis 1.38 or more from the end with a ferrule 2.58 across or less (a wider one moves the column in by half its excess); B16's underside (Z 48.57 at the worst) lies inside the band (Z 46.80..51.78), so both layers meet its edge in plan
  levers, each to be judged with the picked plug: 5G MAIN turned less (no plug lies beyond it); a plug whose ferrule ends 13.58 or less from its axis; IRIDIUM in the back bundle, which leaves at most 2 cables passing under a plug (5G MAIN 2, 5G DIV 1, LORA 1)
  outermost east cable (|Y| 62): its axis at X 176.63 at most, the lane's outer cable at X 173.16: the bundle's S-bend of 3.47 in X at R 13.745 needs 13.37 of run; in the lane by |Y| 95.48 (worst 101.72) against 104.16 (worst 103.28)
  from |Y| 93, the previous issue's outermost east site, it would be in the lane only by |Y| 126.48, 22.32 short of 104.16 at nominal
  the bundle bends down (inner cable R 12.5) from |Y| 104.00, 1.25 beyond the pack group's end (102.75; placed within 1.0) with its full height over it, and goes down at |Y| 115.25..120.23; over the leg's outer face at the worst (|Y| 113.28) its underside is at Z 42.67, above the leg's gusset (below Z 30)
